{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"agent_message","text":"Applying inverse gates directly to the bond-8 target exposes a TensorCircuit QR-backpropagation scalability problem: forward evaluation is fine, but reverse-mode through the enlarged target MPS is unstable/too memory-intensive. I’m switching to the mathematically equivalent native route—evolve the Neel ket as a small-bond `MPSCircuit`, then use TensorCircuit’s built-in MPS projection against the fixed DMRG bra. This preserves the direct MPS overlap and keeps autodiff on the trainable circuit only."}}
